    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Superb penthouse apartment with far reaching views.\n\nStep into a beautifully bright and welcoming entrance hallway featuring elegant ceiling coving, a large Velux window, quality wood effect laminate flooring, a stylish radiator cover and convenient access to a generous storage and hot press area.\n\nDouble glass-panelled doors lead into a spectacular open plan living, kitchen and dining space flooded with natural light from its dual-aspect orientation. The room boasts impressive high ceilings and breathtaking panoramic sea views stretching across Malahide beach to Lambay Island. A feature gas fireplace creates a stunning focal point, while two separate balcony areas provide uninterrupted coastal views including vistas towards The Island Golf Club.\n\nA cleverly designed sunken seating nook comfortably accommodates up to six people and includes integrated underseat storage and atmospheric backlighting, making it a standout feature of the home. Additional bespoke touches include built-in shelving alcoves and a custom seating bench beside the fireplace.\n\nThe newly fitted kitchen is finished with tiled flooring and splashbacks contemporary wall and floor-mounted units, wooden worktops and a stylish breakfast bar with seating for two to three stools. Integrated appliances, a gas range cooker with extractor hood, Velux window and recessed spot lighting complete this exceptional culinary space.\n\nBedroom accommodation comprises three generous double bedrooms. The third bedroom features built-in wardrobes, high ceilings, spotlights and a Velux window. Across the hall, the family bathroom is fully tiled and includes a WC, wash hand basin, bath with overhead shower connection, and a fitted backlit mirror.\n\nThe spacious principal bedroom enjoys built-in wardrobes, a dedicated walk-in wardrobe area with extensive shelving and hanging space, and direct access to a private balcony with magnificent sea views. The ensuite bathroom is stylishly tiled and fitted with a large walk-in rainfall shower, WC, wash hand basin, Velux window, and a striking exposed brick feature wall.\n\nThe second bedroom is another bright double room with built-in wardrobes, radiator cover, large Velux window and a highly practical access hatch to extensive eaves storage, a rare and valuable feature in apartment living.\n\nOverall, 14 The Anchorage is an exceptional coastal residence combining luxurious finishes, clever design features, and some of the finest uninterrupted sea views Malahide has to offer.\n\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall - 4.23m (13'11\") x 1.8m (5'11\")\nWelcoming wide entrance hall with wood flooring, inset spotlights.\n\nOpen Plan Living / Dining / Kitchen\nBright and spacious, dual aspect and sea views. Wood flooring and inset spotlights throughout,\n\nLiving Area - 5.19m (17'0\") x 3.57m (11'9\")\nThe feature fireplace and feature wall sets a focal point for the living space, built in seating, further built in shelving, wood flooring, inset spotlights and access to the balcony with sea views.\n\nBalcony - 1.07m (3'6\") x 2.18m (7'2\")\nWith superb views.\n\nDining Area - 4.29m (14'1\") x 2.9m (9'6\")\nPositioned across from the kitchen, built in table and seating, access to a further balcony\n\nBalcony - 2.19m (7'2\") x 1.01m (3'4\")\nWith far reaching views.\n\nKitchen - 2.23m (7'4\") x 4.57m (15'0\")\nFloor and wall mounted units giving ample storage, built in oven and hob with stainless steel extractor over, subway tiled splashback. Breakfast bar with space for stools. Tiled floor, inset spotlights.\n\nMain Bedroom - 3.16m (10'4\") x 4.56m (15'0\")\nFeature wall, inset spotlights, access to the balcony, inset spotlights.\n\nBalcony - 2.14m (7'0\") x 0.91m (3'0\")\nSea views.\n\nWalk in Wardrobe - 1.71m (5'7\") x 3.3m (10'10\")\nWith extensive shelving and hanging space.\n\nEnsuite - 1.96m (6'5\") x 1.99m (6'6\")\nShower with tiled surround, wash hand basin, WC, heated towel rail, part tiled walls, inset spotlights and rooflight for added light and ventilation.\n\nBedroom Two - 3.76m (12'4\") x 3.06m (10'0\")\nSpacious double room with built in wardrobe, eaves storage, wood flooring, inset spotlights,\n\nBedroom Three - 6.67m (21'11\") x 2.47m (8'1\")\nDouble room with built in wardrobe.\n\nBathroom - 1.96m (6'5\") x 2.48m (8'2\")\nFully tiled with white suite comprising bath with shower over, wash basin set in vanity unit, WC, rooflight.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
